                <pb facs="0211" n="131" sameAs="frus:frus1902/pg131"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Wu to Mr. Hay.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Chinese Legation</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1901-10-25"><hi rendition="#italic">October 25,
                        1901</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 213.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to inclose for your
                    information a translation of a dispatch addressed to me by His Excellency Liu
                    Kun-yih, viceroy at Nanking, relative to a recent rupture at Hsin-Chin between
                    Chinese converts of the American Protestant mission and those of a Roman
                    Catholic mission.</p>
                <p>The unsatisfactory state of things, to which the viceroy calls attention, is due
                    to the indiscriminate assistance rendered by some missionaries to Chinese
                    Christian converts who, relying upon the “protection” of the missions,
                    oftentimes defy the authority of the local officials, whose efforts to preserve
                    peace and promote the general welfare of the people are thus set at naught.</p>
                <p>It is sincerely hoped that the foreign governments concerned and the missionary
                    societies, whose object is to do good in China, will carefully consider the
                    matter and accord to Chinese officials all possible cooperation in their efforts
                    to promote and maintain peaceful and harmonious relations between Chinese
                    Christians of different sects, as well as between Christian and non-Christian
                    Chinese.</p>
                <p>Trusting you will take such action as you may deem proper in the matter, I beg to
                    renew, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Wu Ting-fang</hi>.</signed></closer>


                <xi:include href="d119-a1.xml" xpointer="d119-a1"/>
